          "type": "PARALLEL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prioritize SR Requiring Attention"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773004968321"
          },
          "code": "PRIORITIZE_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION",
          "id": "1773003548258",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773003548260_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Task:\nReview the following inputs:\n\nSR requiring attention List: {{$context.$nodes.SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.SRDetails}}\nCustomer Opportunity / Revenue Information: {{$context.$nodes.GET_OPEN_OPPORTUNITY.$output}}\nCustomer Highest-Severity Open SRs Information: {{$context.$nodes.HIGH_SEVERITY_OPEN_SR_BY_ACCOUNT.$output.result}}\n\nUsing these inputs, prioritize the input SR requiring attention List. If no SR Requiring Attention, return an empty JSON array\n\nInstructions:\nFor each SR in the input, generate a CSM-facing reason that includes:\n1. Why the SR requires attention, make sure to use the Reason attribute from the input for the given SR to explain why it requires attention.\n2. Why the SR is prioritized, based strictly on the prioritization criteria listed below.\n\nImportant constraints:\n- Ensure that **every** SR from the \"SR requiring attention List\" is included in the output\n- Do not include any recommended actions in the explanation.\n- Use only the criteria listed below for prioritization. Emphasize the first three criteria naturally when present. \n- The explanation should be clear, concise, and suitable for a CSM audience.\n\nPrioritization Criteria (Highest → Lowest Priority):\n- Human Safety Threat: The issue poses a potential threat to human safety.\n- Significant Financial Cost: The issue has the potential for significant financial cost to the customer or the implementing company (the higher the cost potential, the higher the priority).\n- Product Usability Impact: The issue renders the product unusable or severely impacts the benefits realized from the product.\n- Multiple Open Escalated SRs: The customer has multiple open SRs that are currently escalated. (the more escalated SRs, the higher the priority).\n- High Severity of Open SRs: The customer has additional open SRs of the highest severity. Refer to the Customer Highest-Severity Open SRs information for the **total** high-severity SRs, excluding the current SR when checking for additional SRs.\n- Significant Near-Term Opportunities: The customer has significant opportunities in progress. Refer to Customer Opportunity / Revenue Information.\n- Multiple Recommended Actions: The SR has multiple recommended actions to perform. This is indicated by ActionCount.\n\n\n\nOutput:\nReturn the Prioritized result in the following JSON format. Ensure that **every** SR from the \"SR requiring attention List\" is included in the output. For each SR, the Reason must clearly combine both the attention reason (from the input Reason attribute) and the prioritization rationale, explaining why the SR requires attention and why it is prioritized based on the criteria listed above.\n\n[\n  {\n    \"SrNumber\": \"<SR1>\",\n    \"Reason\": \"<Brief reason combining why the SR needs attention and the prioritization explanation, following the criteria naturally. Do not repeat ‘Meets’ or ‘Prioritization’ directly.>\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"SrNumber\": \"<SR2>\",\n    \"Reason\": \"<Brief reason combining why the SR needs attention and the prioritization explanation, following the criteria naturally. Do not repeat ‘Meets’ or ‘Prioritization’ directly.>\"\n  },\n // ...add more as appropriate\n]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prioritized SR Requiring Attention",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const attentionSRs = $context.$nodes.PRIORITIZE_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output \nconst compareSRs = $context.$nodes.SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.SRDetails\nconst account = $context.$nodes.FETCH_ALL_ACCOUNT_SCORE.$output.items\n\nconst attentionSRCount = compareSRs.length;\n\n\nconst accountTierMap = new Map(\n  account.map(a => [a.PartyNumber, a.AccountScoringTier])\n);\n\n\nconst allSRs = attentionSRs.map(attentionSR => {\n  const matchingSR = compareSRs.find(compareSR => compareSR.SrNumber === attentionSR.SrNumber);\n  return {\n    ...(matchingSR || {}),\n    Reason: attentionSR.Reason,\n    AccountTier: accountTierMap.get(matchingSR?.AccountPartyNumber) || null\n  };\n});\n\n\nconst top3SRs = allSRs.slice(0, 3);\n\nconst remainingSRs = allSRs.slice(3);\nconst remainingSRCount = remainingSRs.length;\n\n\n\nconst srNumbers = top3SRs\n  .map(s => `\"${s.SrNumber}\"`)\n  .join(',');\n\nconst output = {\n  SRDetails: top3SRs,\n  RemainingSRDetails: remainingSRs,\n  SRNumber: srNumbers,\n  attentionSRCount: attentionSRCount,\n  remainingSRCount: remainingSRCount\n};\n\nreturn output;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769207335237"
          },
          "code": "PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION",
          "id": "1773004968321",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
