        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": true,
              "customNotes": "Set the title of messageListWidget based on the value of \n{{$context.$nodes.PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.attentionSRCount}} (refer to it as <count>).\n\nRules:\n- If <count> = 0, set the title to:\n  \"There are no escalated service requests that require your attention\".\n- If <count> = 1, set the title to:\n  \"{{$context.$nodes.PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.attentionSRCount}} escalated service request requires your attention\".\n- If <count> > 1, set the title to:\n  \"{{$context.$nodes.PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.attentionSRCount}} escalated service requests require your attention\".\nEnsure the grammar and pluralization (\"request\" vs \"requests\", \"requires\" vs \"require\") are correct based on the value of <count>.\n\nDo not populate the description or subtitle fields; leave them empty."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Escalation Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ESCALATION_DETAILS",
          "id": "1769540034859",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769540034861_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "1. Generate a messageListWidget for the first 3 Escalated Service Requests from the following input {{$context.$nodes.PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.SRDetails}}.  Ensure the original input order is preserved in the output list.\n\nFor the first 3 Escalated Service Request in the input, set the following attributes, making sure to include all attributes mentioned below. Do not set status attribute. \n{\n  \"title\": \"<Generate the SR title in this format: <SR Title> (<SRNumber>). For example, if the SR title is 'Solar Inverter Not Exporting Power' and the SR number is 12345, the output should be 'Solar Inverter Not Exporting Power (12345)'.>\",\n   \"subtitle\": \"<AccountPartyUniqueName - 'Tier X' if AccountTier exists; otherwise only show AccountPartyUniqueName. Format AccountTier as 'Tier 1', 'Tier 2', etc. If AccountPartyUniqueName is null, leave subtitle empty.>\"\n   \"summary\": \"<Do not include SR number. In 1–3 concise sentences (maximum 50 words), summarize the issue, focusing on critical or high-impact symptoms and operational risk. Seamlessly incorporate the attention and prioritization reasons from the SR Reason attribute within the sentences so they flow naturally with the issue. Use professional, CSM-facing language. Do not invent new information or include technical details.>\",\n  \"badgeText\": \"<SeverityCdMeaning>\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"<escalationElapsed>\",\n  \"priority\": \"<Set based on SeverityCd Sev1 → alert, Sev2 → warning>\"\n}\n\nSet the title of messageListWidget based on the value of \n{{$context.$nodes.PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.attentionSRCount}} (refer to it as <count>).\n\nRules:\n- If <count> = 0, set the title to:\n  \"There are no escalated service requests that require your attention\".\n- If <count> = 1, set the title to:\n  \"{{$context.$nodes.PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.attentionSRCount}} escalated service request requires your attention\".\n- If <count> > 1, set the title to:\n  \"{{$context.$nodes.PRIORITIZED_SR_REQUIRING_ATTENTION.$output.result.attentionSRCount}} escalated service requests require your attention\".\nEnsure the grammar and pluralization (\"request\" vs \"requests\", \"requires\" vs \"require\") are correct based on the value of <count>.\n\nIMPORTANT: You must not generate any text other than content inside <oraInfoDisplay>, <oraInsight>, and <oraComms> tags.\n\n2. **High Priority Action Insight**\n\nGiven the data `PriorityActionList` {{$context.$variables.priorityActionList}}\n\n## Filter the `PriorityActionList` \n- Collect the Objects which is having Action as \"Reassign\" or \"AddTeamMember\". Do not consider any other Actions.\n- Ignore the Object which is having Action as empty.\n\nGenerate a High Priority Action Insight for each item within the `PriorityActionList` with the following specifications, ensure the original input order is preserved in the output list.\n\n- \"priority\": true (IMPORTANT: MUST set priority to true)\n- \"followUpCommand\": ora.Invoke(\"Review\",{\"action\":\"Review\",\"record\":<PriorityActionList object>})\n- \"shortDescription\": \"<Reason>\",\n- \"actionText\": \"Review\"\n- \"title\": clearly show the SR number and the recommended action. \n- Do not create Priority Insight without priority parameter.\n\nEnsure that the High Priority Action Insight follows the same order as the SR Number listed in the `PriorityActionList` Response.\n\n3. **High Priority Communication**\n\nSR Details: {{$context.$nodes.ESCALATION_COMMUNICATION_FILTER.$output}}\n\nProduce {{$context.$nodes.SHOW_ONLY_SRS_WITH_DEFAULT_CHANNELS.$output.result.length}} high priority (set priority parameter to true) communications <oraComms> with the following details. If no SRs are present, do not produce any output.\nRetrieve the SR number, the reason it requires communication, and the default channel display name from {{$context.$nodes.SHOW_ONLY_SRS_WITH_DEFAULT_CHANNELS.$output.result}}.\n\n- title: <SrNumber>: Generate a short phrase describing the email action required by the Customer Service Manager.\n- shortDescription: the reason it requires communication \n- to: primary contact email address\n- actionText: 'Send Email'\n- type: email\n- subject: a concise and professional email subject line for an escalation communication\n- content: Generate a professional and empathetic email draft from a Customer Service Manager to the customer. The purpose of this email is to offer comfort and reassurance, address any frustrations or concerns shown in the past messages. Where appropriate, acknowledge the customer’s feelings, summarize their main concerns, and describe the actions being taken or next steps. The tone should be professional, polite, and reassuring. You may use the primary contact name in the greeting (e.g., \"Hi [Name],\") at the start of the email body. Include a polite sign-off at the end, followed by the sender's name {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraUserContext.fullName}}. Ensure the email is concise and easy to read — avoid unnecessary details or repetition. Important: Do not include a subject line or any other metadata — output only the email body. The email content must be properly formatted with line breaks and clear paragraphs, and should not be written as one continuous block of text. Generate the output as HTML.\n- \"non editable params\": \n    {\n      { \"id\": \"srNumber\", \"title\": \"SR number\"}\n    }\n- \"editable params\":\nInclude the following editable parameter and make it required\n    {\n      { \"id\": \"channelDisplayName\", \"title\": \"Channel Display Name\"}\n    }\n\n- \"priority\": true (IMPORTANT: MUST set priority to true)\n\nYou **must** generate srNumber and channelDisplayName parameters and assign them their corresponding values. \nIMPORTANT: Set the targetAgent of the communication to {{$context.$workflow.$name}} and set priority to true."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
